Z||000000||Bill 88||08-14-2000||11:18 AM||||I read in one of the posts about the lock not-working and getting into the trunk another way.  Can yu explain this to me?  I did not know that there was another way to get in.  <BR>P.S. I can not find the post either.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||08-14-2000||01:21 PM||||I believe the alternative was to drill out the lock cylinder.  The person tried it and was surprised at how easy it was and at how little damage it caused.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||08-14-2000||01:27 PM||||Yeah, that was me...lock stopped working and I drilled it out with a 1/4 inch tool steel drill in a hammer drill.<P>Took about 30 seconds...no damage other than to the lock.<P>I did find another lock (with a key) at the boneyard for $1.<P>The locks on these cars are probably no better or worse than those on any other cars.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||08-14-2000||01:42 PM||||Sorry if this sounds a little elementary to many, but I'm not sure if this is the other way those guys were talking about.  Another way you could open the rear deck is through the rear deck release button on the dash.  If you don't have one or it doesn't work, then I guess your out'a luck.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 08-14-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||wla21841||08-20-2000||03:03 PM||||I have lock my keys in the trunck several times. I have a small screw driver and 2 foot jumper wire in the car for this porpose.<BR>You unascrew the head light switch and the trunk switch and juper the hot on the light switch and the trunk switch. Bingo the trunk opens. It allways happened when I am in a hurry.||||reg||1
